A||||6||BAM-BAM||Mass air sensor?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-27-2000||08:14 AM||||  I am having a problem with idle surge. Only<BR>when I am in park or neutral and at idle,the engine rpm runs up and down between 800-1000<BR>rpm. It causes me no problems other than it's annoying. I replaced the IAC but that hasn't given any improvement in "THAT" area. I have noticed a smoother idle otherwise(MIND TRICK?) I was wondering if it could be the mass air sensor. I have heard that a problem there could belay these symptoms. any info Helpful <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||03-27-2000||12:38 PM||||Try disconnecting your battery for a while. Let the ECM relearn your engine, with the new valve.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-27-2000||12:48 PM||||Fiero doesn't use a mass air sensor. V6 and 87-88 4 cyl do use an air temperature sensor. It's in the air filter can on V6 and the right side top of the intake manifold on the 4. Make sure that it's not dirty or corroded.<P>Did you also check for vacuum leaks? Did you disconnect and plug the ports for the fuel vapor canister? (Plug them on the engine.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||03-27-2000||11:21 PM||||   Theorge,<BR>   What should I expect when I disconnect and plug the ports from the fuel vapor cannister? I appologize for my apparent ignorance; I am learning more all the time.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>  Raydar, <BR>  Thanks, I had the battery disconnected when I change the IAC valve. We'll see, I'll try it again.<P>  Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000004||theogre||03-27-2000||11:36 PM||||The vapor canister is only supposed to "purge" under certain conditions. If the purge valve is stuck or damaged then you have a vac leak and/or rich mix depending on how much vapor is trapped in the can. Plugging the lines at the manifold eliminates the can and both it's lines from being souces of problems. Under normal conditions the can has no effect on performance if it's connected or not.  If the can or it's lines are messed up fix them. This device causes no performance penalty but does prevent a major source of air polution. When it's working right it can actually help fuel millage. (It keeps vapor in your gas tank going to the motor instead of the atmosphere)<P>Note: if cruise control shares one of the lines with the vapor can then cruise will not work durring this test.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ironhorse||03-28-2000||03:25 PM||||BAM,  I have a 89 Ford Probe LX (I know I know, I'm in a process of getting rid of it so I can buy a Fiero) anyway on my car it used to do the same thing. On the 4 cyc motor one of my sparkplug and wire was bad, after I replaced the plug and wire that was bad.  No more rpm jumping up and down at idle.  Look for a bad wire or sparkplug.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||03-28-2000||09:52 PM||||   Thanks guys for the input, I will take it all in and surely a solution will come. This is  the coolest place on earth. No mechanic at a dealership or auto house will share the kind of info the forum shares. <P> Thanks again, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
